A||||3||deceler8||Body Panel Fasteners...where to get 'em||||5
Z||000000||deceler8||09-22-1999||05:53 PM||||Am I correct that there is a kind of plastic "rivet" that holds some of the stuff on my car ('86 2m4) ?<P>Seems several are missing from one of my rocker panels. What are they called and where can I get them ? And what can be used as a substitute if they're not available ?<P>Sorry if this has already been covered. Tried searching for this info but didn't come up with any matches.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-22-1999||05:58 PM||||Did you try calling your local GM dealer for the plastic rivets???? I know they are expensive..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-22-1999||08:06 PM||||When I added the GT clip to my car, I had to drill out a lot of the plastic rivits, but I found a cheap alternative. I went to a ACE hardware and got some plastic drywall anchors- they look like a white plastic rivit with a steel pin in the middle. I put a steel washer under the head of the anchor to make them fit tight and they worked great. Very cheap too!||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-23-1999||10:26 AM||||MotorMite packages these in the BodyTite and RivetTite blister packs available at most PEP-Boys and other outlets.<P>I prefer to use "screw rivets" where posible. These have a plastic screw that expands the ears. The ones for the door skin are Rivet-tite number 47954. These are 1/4 inch diam. looks like they should work the rockers. Might be the rockers are a size smaller. BTW these are black and match the rocker material. They run about $1.50 us per pack. These are also reentrant should you ever need to open it up again, like to change a smashed rocker.||||reg||1
